<ProjectLayout slug="vis-a-vis-verification">

  <p>
  The process of “vis-a-vis verification” is fundamentally concerned<br />
  with the way in which relationships of trust are established within a system.
</p>

<p>
  For this, it is necessary that a real social interaction takes place<br />
  between an already verified person and a person newly added to the system;<br />
  that is, both individuals stand “vis-a-vis,” face to face with one another,<br />
  and perform a specific action.
</p>

<p>
  Not all individuals can be incorporated into the feedback loop.<br />
  Some are too fragile and risk breaking,<br />
  while others are too strong and could cause something to break.
</p>

<p>
  These forms of becoming presuppose that, in a moment of experience,<br />
  bodies pass through the feeling that it could suddenly all be over<br />
  at the ends of the world or of human beings.
</p>

